Year = {2026},
Volume = {58},
Number = {228},
Pages = {786-803},
Month = {SUM},
Abstract = {The study analyzes the soundscape (SS) of Torre d'en Dol \& ccedil;a
   Park, a transitional space between the tourist core of Vila-seca and
   Salou, and the South Tarragona petrochemical complex within the
   metropolitan area of Tarragona (Spain), with the aim of providing a
   multisensory perspective on urban design and planning. Methodologically,
   qualitative and quantitative techniques with a phenomenological approach
   were applied, combining observation, questionnaires, sound walks, and
   spectrographic analysis. The results indicate that the SS integrates
   natural and human sound sources alongside mechanical sounds, such as
   motor vehicle traffic, industry, trains, and the activities of
   PortAventura park. These external sounds, although not exceeding 55
   dB(A), are intrusive and affect the recreational, leisure, and health
   experience of users.},
